# What Cursor must not read when the workbench runs it in this folder.
#
# A file Cursor opens itself goes to Cursor's servers as it is -- WITHOUT
# the redaction the workbench applies to the prompts it writes (hosts,
# tokens, passwords removed: tools/agent/design.py redact). Until this file
# existed, only a sentence in the prompt ("never open
# program_configuration*.json") kept the credentials out. Same syntax as
# .gitignore. tools/agent/test_cursorignore.py checks every secret file the
# .gitignore names is here too.

# Credentials: one configuration file a project, and the Cursor key.
src/main/resources/program_configuration.json
src/main/resources/program_configuration.goal.json
program_configuration.json
program_configuration.goal.json
cursor_agent.json
**/cursor_agent.json
tools/ra_converter/cursor_agent.json
**/cursor_agent.local.json

# Any other secret file the .gitignore keeps out of git.
*.env
.env
application-secret.properties
application-local.properties
src/main/resources/application-local.properties
src/test/resources/application-local.properties
src/main/resources/application-*.properties
src/test/resources/application-*.properties
!src/main/resources/application-qa.properties
**/*SET_c_id_*
src/main/resources/config/qa.json
src/main/resources/config/prod.json
**/credentials.properties
**/*-credentials.properties
src/main/resources/templates/tokenrequest.json

# The workbench's own state: job logs, Jira and Confluence copies, the
# server's logs. A job's brief and plan reach Cursor in the prompt, redacted.
.workbench/

# Build output and run logs (request and response bodies of real calls).
# The ReadyAPI suites a convert read stay readable: answering open
# questions searches them for an endpoint.
target/*
!target/convert-input/

# The project's own Python, if made by the launcher.
.venv/
